English translation of the original Japanese commit message:

fix(napi): reject PE dependencies outside the Windows allowlist

Add pe-dependency-policy.mjs to accept only seven documented Windows
DLLs and api-ms-win-* API sets, comparing names case-insensitively. The
old denylist passed unrecognized bundled dependencies such as
libc++.dll, libunwind.dll, and ggml-*.dll. Forbidden MSVC and inference
runtime patterns override the allowlist, even if added by mistake. New
entries require evidence that Windows provides the DLL. Invalid inputs
and zero readable imports still fail. Add policy tests and five
synthetic-PE CLI cases for allowed imports, user32.dll, libc++.dll,
delayed VCRUNTIME140.dll, and empty imports. The existing per-push CI
job now protects the release check with these tests.
